Description: real-time beat clock over JACK, sent as OSC
 Tracks the tempo of a JACK input (BTrack), follows an external clock or a
 Pioneer Pro DJ Link master; sends /beat as OSC to the targets in its
 config. It does not meter: the A3 engine measures /vu. Works with any JACK
 server, PipeWire's included, and needs nothing else of the A3 system.
 .
 Runs as the systemd user unit beat-analyzer.service, which is not enabled
 on install: systemctl --user enable --now beat-analyzer. The config is
 ~/.config/beat-analyzer/beat-analyzer.env, made from the shipped example
 on the first start and never written over; files in its conf.d/ follow
 it, a later one winning. It stays when the package is removed or purged.

